			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> react and tailwind have some of the most toxic community I've seen in tech that almost feel like cults. The way react sold the notion that SPAs are faster than traditional client-server apps, tailwind also sold that utility-first css ship less styles than semantic css. <br>Both the lies have been debunked, but the fanboys are too stubborn to accept the fact.</p>",
